# Agent runtime

An agent is a software system with a goal, inputs, outputs, model, state, context, memory, tools, permissions, lifecycle, timeout, cancellation, retries, failure behavior, approval gates, a security boundary, observability, evaluation, and cost controls.

Context is selected. Do not dump the full history, corpus, and tool catalog into every call.

Tools validate arguments before side effects. Retrieved text, web pages, files, and tool output do not gain policy or permission authority.

Add another agent only for specialization, isolated context, separate permissions, independent review, real parallelism, or a separate failure domain. Define ownership, handoff contracts, cancellation, and failure propagation.

Human approval sits in the runtime for irreversible or privileged actions, not only in the prompt.
